WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:02.606
Rosa is going home from hospital.

2
00:00:02.606 --> 00:00:07.116
Her medicines have changed: one stopped, one dose raised, one new.

3
00:00:07.966 --> 00:00:14.089
Usually that news travels by letter, and is typed again at the pharmacy and at her doctor's practice.

4
00:00:14.089 --> 00:00:16.090
Mistakes happen at each retyping.

5
00:00:16.940 --> 00:00:19.631
Rosa's medication list is in her pod.

6
00:00:20.481 --> 00:00:25.108
On the ward, the pharmacist records the three changes, with a reason for each.

7
00:00:25.108 --> 00:00:30.329
The list is written once, in a standard health format, where everyone else will read it.

8
00:00:31.179 --> 00:00:32.903
Rosa decides who can see it.

9
00:00:33.753 --> 00:00:36.672
Her pharmacy can read her medicines and allergies.

10
00:00:36.672 --> 00:00:40.174
Her doctor's practice can read and update her health record.

11
00:00:40.174 --> 00:00:43.967
Her son, Alex, can read the list, because he helps with her care.

12
00:00:44.817 --> 00:00:48.866
The pharmacist opens the list and sees what changed since the last supply.

13
00:00:49.716 --> 00:00:51.884
They dispense, and record it in the pod.

14
00:00:52.734 --> 00:00:55.247
The pharmacy saw medicines and allergies.

15
00:00:55.247 --> 00:00:57.514
It did not see the discharge summary.

16
00:00:58.366 --> 00:01:01.553
A week later, Rosa's doctor opens the same list.

17
00:01:02.403 --> 00:01:03.598
They stop a duplicate.

18
00:01:03.598 --> 00:01:07.784
That change is written to the same record, with the doctor's name against it.

19
00:01:08.634 --> 00:01:10.788
The pharmacy sees it on its next read.

20
00:01:10.788 --> 00:01:13.963
The practice and the pharmacy never exchanged a message.

21
00:01:14.811 --> 00:01:18.311
And Alex sees the current list in his own wallet, read-only.

22
00:01:19.161 --> 00:01:23.602
Rosa moves to a pharmacy nearer home, and withdraws the old one's access.

23
00:01:24.452 --> 00:01:26.125
Its next read is refused.

24
00:01:26.125 --> 00:01:29.337
It keeps its own dispensing records, as it must.

25
00:01:29.337 --> 00:01:31.479
It no longer sees the live list.

26
00:01:32.328 --> 00:01:37.579
One list, three organisations writing to it, every change signed with a name and a reason.

27
00:01:38.428 --> 00:01:43.450
If your organisation works with health data, help us shape this one.

28
00:01:43.450 --> 00:01:46.552
Join the EDMA Solid Community of Practice.
